Also ℓ=3 would need group size≥6 with at least 3 common candidates. Do we have such? Voters 4-7 size4 only. Voters 2,3,8,9,10 size5 have 3 common (x1,x2,x3) but need size≥6, not satisfied. So ℓ max 2.

Thus any committee of 5 must contain at least 2 from X-set and at least 2 from Y-set (y4-6). That's 4 slots, leaving 1 free could be any candidate.

Now we need to consider voter1's approved set: {x1,x2,x3,y1,z3}. Intersection with required sets: includes x1,x2,x3 (three candidates) but not y4-6. y1 is not required. So voter1's approved candidates are three X's, plus y1, z3.

Committee must have at least 2 of the X's, could be any of x1,x2,x3. Could also include y1 or z3 if chosen as the extra slot.

