Could we have only 1 approved? To have only 1 from X's, we would need only one X candidate, but then we would violate the requirement of at least 2 X's. So min cannot be 1. Could we have 0? No.

Thus min =2.

Now max number of voter1 approved candidates in committee. Voter1 approves 5 candidates total. Committee size 5, but must include at least 2 Y's (y4-6) which voter1 does NOT approve. So at most 3 of voter1's approved can be in committee (the three X's). Could we also include y1 (approved) as the fifth? Wait we need 2 Y's from y4-6, that's two slots. The remaining three slots could be x1,x2,x3 (all approved) giving total 3 approved. Could we also include y1 instead of one of the Y's? No, because we must have at least 2 of y4-6. So we need those two slots occupied by y4 and y5 (or y6). Those are not approved. So max approved = 3 (x1,x2,x3). Could we also include z3? That would be a fourth approved, but would require dropping one of the required Y's, violating EJR. So max =3.

